      "question_excerpt": "Andy walks 50 meters from his house to school. After school, he comes back to the house and goes to the market. If he walks 140 meters in total, how many meters is the distance between the house and the market?",
      "reference_answer": "40",
      "selected_answer": "45",
      "interpretation": "The return from school to home is another 50 m, so 50+50+x=140 gives x=40. The selected trace instead sets the return leg to x and solves 50+2x=140, obtaining 45. Its algebra is consistent with the wrong equation; the error is assigning the route quantities. Three traces state 40, but two lack a recognized final-answer marker; official parses are None, 45, 40, None. The valid comparison is therefore one candidate per answer group. A large score margin does not certify semantic correctness.",
